    "js": "proof.waitFor(() => { const view = document.querySelector('[data-type=\"discourse-context-view\"]'); const match = view && /Content:\\s*([^\\n]+)/.exec(view.innerText); return match && match[1].trim() === \"NCT - why do we sleep\"; }, { what: \"Content: NCT - why do we sleep\" })",
    "text": "Content shows the whole title, NCT - why do we sleep. Before this PR it showed why do we sleep. This is the PR's open scope decision."
  },
  "checks": "The note in the PK No Content type (`NCT - {question}`) shows Content: NCT - why do we sleep, the whole title. Before this PR it showed why do we sleep.",
  "caption": "The one declared change: a format with a placeholder but no content placeholder now shows the whole title."
}
```

Note the layering: `js` = machine assertion, `text` = human-readable claim, `checks` = plain-English restatement for the live panel, `caption` = video narration, `proves` = traceability to the ticket.

**How it runs**

- Roam: install the runner extension by URL (`https://discoursegraphs.com/releases/prototypes/proof-runner/`), open the kit page, press Run.
- Obsidian: `node obsidian/dist/cli.mjs --kit k.json --worktree <dg worktree> --marker <str> [--pause failure] [--pace 1]` (`obsidian/cli.ts:2-4`), driving Obsidian over CDP.

**What it outputs** — `obsidian/cli.ts` `runOnce()` writes into `<worktree>/local/proof-kit/<branch>/<kit>-<timestamp>/`:
- `result.md` — the PR comment
- `kit-report.md` — fixes needed in the kit itself
- `records.json` — per-case records
- `journal.jsonl`, `added-cases.jsonl`
- `screenshots/` (the `screenshot` action)

`result.md` shape (`src/roam/words.ts:433-507`):

```
**Proof run: 5 of 7 passed, 1 failed, 1 couldn't be tested**
PR #1508 build obsidian-runner @ a1b2c3d (the PR's latest) · 2026-10-08 14:02 · on failure, 1× in Obsidian (slot-2)

Done When (ENG-2176)
- [x] 1. `Claim (draft) - {content}` matches its titles… (2 cases)
- [ ] 2. One shared, unit-tested implementation… (1 case, failed)

Failed
- Case 3: Obsidian publishes the same content its Content line shows. …

Couldn't be tested
- Case 6: …

Left out by the tester
- Case 7: …  The tester said: "…"

The kit needs 2 fixes, listed on the proof page under runs.
Not tested: 1, with reasons on the proof page.
```

There is also a bug-report formatter, `words.ts:509-521`, fixed shape: `Problem / Expected / Observed / Steps / Evidence`.

In Roam, a finished run also appends to the page's `runs::` list: verdicts, build, commit, time, who ran it.

